#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096444 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "e47a8da7-9276-5f4c-8ee6-1fd737c2e9ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-4277" :question/problem "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](images/04/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/53/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/81/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/id #uuid "0b0dbbc1-d39d-5aff-9f16-075779d36659" :question/math-academy-id "e-5015" :question/problem "![](images/24/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" :question/worked-solution "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}.$\n\n- Equality II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}-\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{AC}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "c7526e18-37a9-572a-a6a3-0384bbccf41d" :question/math-academy-id "e-9934" :question/problem "![](images/74/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/49/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/08/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367788ba-9c7c-5e7c-8d21-94b3c4ba0009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244796} {:answer/id #uuid "8f148817-c745-530a-a8b8-28d7b5e4345e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=c-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245562} {:answer/id #uuid "b417d004-817e-5033-a8fd-22b425d08539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a-b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245918} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e4a15b-18c4-5947-9ba2-a025c8d4e9c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a+b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245957} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bce547-b8ee-520e-ad41-e9f53f4bdc96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d+a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367788ba-9c7c-5e7c-8d21-94b3c4ba0009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244796} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdcf588e-a428-59ae-a4f9-9b453b8f13ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4193f1f9-5dd6-5e42-ab53-c9d471fede26" :question/math-academy-id "q-11323" :question/problem "![](images/36/36aaf58af536428c74cdb8f4c02c2b4f07e414422e8aea378c75d7abcff58cff.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{YX}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{XV}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{VZ}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{XW}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $X$ to $W$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$  \n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XW}=\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW},\n$$\n\nas shown below. \n\n![](images/47/4758b51fd3dc076059d60e944de0ad8375bb304240365959d4c6cae94f95a535.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XY}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/e9/e942d61c1f51c36dc6cd04f88ff5e37f538920a34c1af5bc780c47691567b668.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{XW} & =\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW} \\\\  & =-a+d \\\\  & =d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/i